# Always use the LSC Delivery Architect for LSC work

Whenever the user asks to **create, write, draft, plan, refactor, break down,
migrate, or prototype** a solution, user story, requirement, build spec,
technical specification, epic, or product-owner-facing mockup for **Salesforce
Life Sciences Cloud (LSC)**, you MUST first read and follow the skill at
`.cursor/skills/lsc-delivery-architect/SKILL.md` (the "LSC Delivery Architect",
formerly the "LSC User Story Solution Architect" through v1.7), and author the
output using its contract.

## Triggers (non-exhaustive)

- "create/write/draft a user story", "story for …", "US-…", "acceptance criteria"
- "break down this into stories", "epic", "decompose the spec"
- "refactor story", "bug fix story", "build spec", "implementation plan"
- **Plan + Prototype (no stories yet):** "plan and prototype", "plan + prototype",
  "plan only", "just a plan", "solution plan", "prototype only", "prototype first",
  "no stories yet", "not ready for stories"
- **Salesforce-grounded HTML prototype**, "clickable prototype", "clickable mockup",
  "PO mockup", "walkthrough for the product owner"
- **LSC-specific:** Visits/Calls, Sample Management, Product Item & Production
  Batch inventory, Territory & Cycle Plans, Action Launcher, Assessments, Medical
  Inquiry, Consent, KOL/DOL, **SAP Concur expense integration** (visit & event
  expenses, expense reports, estimated allocation, MuleSoft expense sync), and
  **Veeva CRM → Salesforce LSC migration**.

## Non-negotiables from the skill (hard blockers)

- **Concrete business persona** — never "user"/"business user"/"developer". Use the
  LSC role (e.g., Field Sales Representative, Medical Science Liaison (MSL), Key
  Account Manager (KAM), Event Organizer, LSC Admin, Market Access analyst). HCPs
  are the subject of the interaction, not the login persona.
- **Given / When / Then in business language** (Pattern A) for behavioural ACs — no
  Apex class names, IP versions/step numbers, SOQL, or API field names inside the AC.
  *(Skipped only in Plan + Prototype mode, which produces no ACs.)*
- **`## Technical Implementation (high-level)`** section after the ACs (all
  implementation detail lives here, not in the ACs).
- **Pattern E per-object field spec** on every "records created/updated" outcome —
  every field enumerated, no "etc.".
- **Declarative-first build-technology decision** (RULE 7a) — prefer OOTB Lightning
  + Dynamic Actions / Screen Flow / Field Sets before OmniScript; OmniStudio is
  one option, not the default.
- **Grounded HTML prototype rule (§6.7)** — a PO prototype MUST label every element
  with its Salesforce component (OOTB / Config / Flow / LWC / OmniScript / Apex /
  Ext). An unlabelled generic web mockup is not acceptable.
- **Never hallucinate component names** — verify custom components via
  `code-review-graph` and standard LSC objects/fields via `salesforce-docs` first,
  and scan `requirements/` for overlapping stories.
- Include the required sections in canonical order and an **Estimated Effort** table.

## If the MCP is available

If an LSC Delivery Architect MCP server is connected, you may use it. If it is
unavailable, fall back to the skill file above — do not skip the Architect contract.
